&lt;p&gt;Let $P_n$ be the regular $n$-sided polygon – or &lt;dfn&gt;shape&lt;/dfn&gt; – whose vertices 

$w_k$ ($k = 1, 2, \dots, n$) have coordinates:&lt;/p&gt;
\begin{align}
a_k &amp;amp;= \cos((3k - 2)/n \times 180^\circ)\\
b_k &amp;amp;= \sin((3k - 2)/n \times 180^\circ)
\end{align}

&lt;p&gt;Each $P_n$ is to be interpreted as a filled shape consisting of all points on the perimeter and in the interior.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Minkowski difference&lt;/strong&gt;, $P - Q$, of two shapes $P$ and $Q$ is the result of subtracting every point in $Q$ from every point in $P$, where point subtraction is performed coordinate-wise: $(u, v) - (x, y) = (u - x, v - y)$.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, the difference of $P_4$ and $P_5$ is the nine-sided shape shown in blue below:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
&lt;img src=&#34;resources/images/0229.png?1678992053&#34; class=&#34;dark_img&#34; alt=&#34;picture showing P_4 - P_5&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How many sides does $P_{2021} - P_{2022} - \cdots - P_{2066}$ have?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The mathematical operation known as &lt;strong&gt;hyperexponentiation&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;tetration&lt;/strong&gt; of a number $a$ by a positive integer $b$ is symbolized as $a\mathbin{\uparrow \uparrow}b$ or $^b a$. It is defined recursively as follows:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
$a \mathbin{\uparrow \uparrow} 1 = a$,&lt;br&gt;
$a \mathbin{\uparrow \uparrow} (k+1) = a^{(a \mathbin{\uparrow \uparrow} k)}$.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
For instance, $3 \mathbin{\uparrow \uparrow} 2 = 3^3 = 27$, which leads to $3 \mathbin{\uparrow \uparrow} 3 = 3^{27} = 7625597484987$ and $3 \mathbin{\uparrow \uparrow} 4$ approximating to $10^{3.6383346400240996 \cdot 10^{12}}$.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Given this, your task is to determine the last $8$ digits of $1777 \mathbin{\uparrow \uparrow} 1855$, requiring you to apply the principles of hyperexponentiation and modular arithmetic.&lt;/p&gt;

